##
    A lending desk, built on a project of books.

    The reference is what makes Book usable here without this project listing the folder it
    lives in. Books decides what it is made of; Library says only that it builds on Books. Move
    a file inside Books and nothing here changes, which is the whole reason the line is worth
    writing instead of another 'source'.

    A second program wanting books would write the same one line. That is the difference
    between a reference and a source: a source claims files, a reference builds on a project.
##

project Library
    reference books/books.pcp
    source Program.pc
end project
